{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: e60e603ce2f57fd0a3a85ef39c024f18533513a9 (132 artifacts, note notes/2026-09-06-atseq-spike-results.md first), corrected S6 against verdict d8df2a0e.\n\nThe three required changes are closed and each has a regression that fails under mutation. (1) A browser import now checks the archive against every pinned invitation for its DID before any store write, and opening an app re-pins; a forged same-DID genesis is rejected with \"Archive differs from the pinned invitation\" when the device holds an invitation, and the Playwright regression proves the invitation and selection survive reload. (2) The evaluator honours its timeoutMs parameter; replay-class calls pass 120 s, previews keep 15 s; the timer-back-to-15 s mutant fails the test. (3) Acceptance writes a running status before the first command, every log unconditionally, and a complete report with recommendation incomplete on any failure; the report script refuses an incomplete run and checks retainedHashes on a pass; three mutants (no pre-write, copy only on pass, dropped incomplete check) each fail the test. The S5 inherited defect is gone with fe418e89 in the ancestry.\n\nReproduced at the head: check 0 errors; archive 12/12; full suite 283/283; acceptance 13/13 with all exit codes 0. Evidence verified against HEAD bytes: sourceHashes in all 13 experiment reports (0 mismatches); 13/13 log hashes; 13/13 retainedHashes; host-before equals host-after and all 51 hashes match source or host-build; verification.json 22 adapter calls, 5 entries; performance p50/p95 recomputed from raw samples equal the recorded figures; regenerating the note from the retained JSON is byte-identical. No secrets in retained files.\n\nArchitecture: archive, browser shell, evaluator, host sync and acceptance scripts; contracts preserved, docs/archives.md and docs/evolution.md updated in the same head. Security: the pin check is the trust boundary and is exercised before any write; first-import bootstrap trust remains a documented design choice, and after such an import the real invitation can never be opened on that device because there is no unpin path. Simplification: the removed activation closure comparison was dead (load.ts already rejects out-of-closure blocks) and the toBytes replacement is byte-identical and unpadded.\n\nNon-blocking, for the next request: tests/evaluator.test.ts would hang rather than fail if the default budget were raised (add a test timeout); the two new 503 branches in src/host/application.ts (collect error, transport over 16 MiB) have no test, and a 64 by 512 KiB closure exceeds the 16 MiB transport bound so an activation-key holder can make sync return 503 permanently; the CLI pins only when both app and genesis are given; the bound mutations in tests/archive.test.ts use a matcher-less assert.rejects; check-author and retainedHashes are script-checked only.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:34e27e757db55e3b1ca14efae80b0deb8a7ded98","head":"e60e603ce2f57fd0a3a85ef39c024f18533513a9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:9e703c4762039865dca24ca8096fe90bf1a12356\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:9e703c4762039865dca24ca8096fe90bf1a12356","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}